See reproduce.zip
Expected Behavior
When the user explicitly provides -arch or -gencode flags via extra_cuda_cflags, load_inline should not append default legacy -gencode flags.
Ideally, there would be an option (e.g. use_default_gencode=False) or a way to fully override or remove the default list, so only the user-specified architecture flags are used.
Suggested Fix
Add a parameter to load_inline or CUDAExtension, for example:
load_inline(..., default_gencode=False)
When default_gencode=False, do not inject any default -gencode flags. Alternatively, provide a flag like remove_default_cflags=True that filters out the internal defaults.
